        <bannerTitle>
      <Value Culture="en-US"><![CDATA[Blog Details]]></Value>
    </bannerTitle>
                        <contentBlocks>
      <Value Culture="en-US"><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000002",
      "key": "29a5d61d-4386-47be-bea8-f5cbabe5613e",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "At its core, this is a structural problem. Peak academic cycles expose the gaps that normal operations don’t typically show, and without the right support model in place, those gaps will become wider.</p>\n<p>More institutions are turning to outsourcing education services to keep their operations from collapsing under the weight of predictable demand, and here’s why.</p>\n</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000004",
      "key": "dd87da66-4bd1-413b-b153-be04465f4e6a",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "heading",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Application Volume No Longer Predicts Enrollment Outcomes"
        },
        {
          "alias": "level",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "[\"h2\"]"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorId",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000002",
      "key": "f7c01d13-f844-463d-94ce-cc7ae747a0d0",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Student enrollment management</strong> operates on a fixed annual rhythm. Application windows open, review periods compress into shorter timeframes, financial aid packages go out, and orientation logistics converge—all within the same narrow window.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The data shows what happens when that rhythm outpaces institutional capacity.<a href=\"https://www.commonapp.org/files/DAR/deadline-updates/Common-App-End-of-Season-Report_24-25.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> </a><a href=\"https://www.commonapp.org/files/DAR/deadline-updates/Common-App-End-of-Season-Report_24-25.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Common Application&#8217;s 2024–25 End of Season Report</a> recorded first-year applications surpassing 10 million for the first time, an 8% increase over the prior year.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Over the same period, <a href=\"https://nscresearchcenter.org/final-fall-enrollment-trends/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the National Student Clearinghouse’s latest enrollment report</a> found that private nonprofit four-year institutions saw undergraduate enrollment decline by 1.6% in fall 2025.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The explanation for that gap is operational. A<a href=\"https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2426604122\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> </a><a href=\"https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2426604122\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">peer-reviewed study published in PNAS</a>, drawing on data from 274,316 students, found that delays in admissions decisions lead prospective students to abandon their preferred institutions and accept offers from other institutions.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000004",
      "key": "19d5d58d-983a-4cd1-8766-9d748981b31f",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "heading",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Staff Are Already Stretched Before Peak Season Even Starts"
        },
        {
          "alias": "level",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "[\"h2\"]"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorId",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000002",
      "key": "7bd8051c-7118-4318-9889-d34ae975f18f",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The teams responsible for <strong>academic operations</strong> during peak cycles are already running at reduced capacity before the crunch even begins.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Higher education administrative staff have likely been absorbing additional responsibilities for years, with little structural adjustment to account for the cumulative load, forcing other employees to support this workload.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://www.cupahr.org/resource/higher-ed-employee-retention-survey-findings-september-2025/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The 2025 CUPA-HR Higher Education Employee Retention Survey</a> found that 61% of education employees have taken on duties outside their original job descriptions, and 53% have absorbed the responsibilities of departed colleagues who were never replaced. Half of all staff report that their workload regularly generates anxiety or stress.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The retention data reflects the toll.<a href=\"https://www.cupahr.org/surveys/research-briefs/higher-ed-employee-retention-survey-findings-september-2023/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> </a><a href=\"https://www.cupahr.org/surveys/research-briefs/higher-ed-employee-retention-survey-findings-september-2023/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CUPA-HR&#8217;s 2023 Employee Retention Survey</a> documented voluntary turnover reaching its highest point since the organization began tracking it in 2017–18, with exempt staff at 14.3% and nonexempt staff at 15.2%.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This trend is echoed in employee sentiment. <a href=\"https://www.campussafetymagazine.com/news/college-faculty-burnout-the-statistics-and-solutions/132000/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">A national survey by TimelyCare</a> found that more than half (53%) of higher education staff had considered leaving their positions because of burnout, increased workload, and sustained stress.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000004",
      "key": "033af2fd-4766-4fd0-975a-e5276d965e00",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "heading",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "The Same Four Functions Fall Behind Every Single Cycle"
        },
        {
          "alias": "level",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "[\"h2\"]"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorId",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000002",
      "key": "04f1334f-f542-4369-b418-c5b8723873c3",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When enrollment demand surges and staffing capacity stays flat, the strain concentrates in the functions that carry the highest volume and require the most consistent human attention.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here are the four core functions most affected:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Application processing</strong>: Review queues accumulate faster than teams can clear them. <a href=\"https://centrocdx.com/reducing-wait-times-increasing-loyalty-the-cx-impact-of-contact-center-outsourcing/\">Response timelines</a> stretch from days to weeks, and prospective students who receive no word choose institutions that do respond.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Financial aid communications</strong>: Understaffed offices push award letters past the point where competing institutions have already secured commitments, and students who needed a decision last week have already moved on.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Student inquiry management</strong>:<a href=\"https://www.insidehighered.com/news/workplace/staff-issues/2024/09/26/burnout-administrative-staff-risks-destabilizing-colleges\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> </a><a href=\"https://www.insidehighered.com/news/workplace/staff-issues/2024/09/26/burnout-administrative-staff-risks-destabilizing-colleges\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Research reported in Inside Higher Ed</a> found that more than 67% of administrative staff experience frequent, disruptive interruptions during their working day, and more than half regularly work past ten hours. Staff managing that level of workload can’t maintain the consistent, timely communication that prospective students require.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Document processing and transcript evaluation</strong>: Transfer applicants face the longest delays, as manual transcript evaluation slows processing and often forces staff to work overtime just to keep up with weekly demand.</li>\n</ul>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000004",
      "key": "26a66958-51ee-4c65-a7e2-329db9ff1ffe",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "heading",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Full-Time Headcount Can&#8217;t Solve a Seasonal Problem"
        },
        {
          "alias": "level",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "[\"h2\"]"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorId",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000002",
      "key": "7f621ef8-da4a-4ef2-9461-6b481632fb64",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The timing of peak demand in higher education is not unpredictable. Fall enrollment, spring registration, summer orientation, and financial aid processing windows follow the same calendar every year.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The operational strain they produce is a known quantity, and institutions that treat it as an annual emergency are making a structural choice, even if they don’t frame it that way.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Staffing for peak demand leaves teams underutilized most of the year and burned out when it matters most.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Maintaining a reduced headcount controls costs, but it inevitably leads to operational strain whenever volume increases.Workflow automation helps at the margins, but it optimizes process flow, not human capacity.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">So, when the underlying team is already stretched thin, automation accelerates the arrival of work that nobody has the bandwidth to complete.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://centrocdx.com/bpo/\"><strong>Outsourcing education services</strong></a> addresses what neither hiring nor technology resolves on its own: external capacity calibrated to demand rather than fixed to headcount.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Education BPO services</strong> allow institutions to scale support through peak periods without carrying that overhead year-round. With <a href=\"https://www.grandviewresearch.com/industry-analysis/business-process-outsourcing-bpo-market\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the global BPO market reaching an estimated USD 328 billion in 2025</a> and growing at nearly 10% annually, it’s clear that organizations across sectors are arriving at the same conclusion.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For higher education, the practical advantage is continuity. An external partner already familiar with an institution&#8217;s processes, systems, and communication standards doesn’t need to be rebuilt from scratch each fall. The knowledge carries forward, and the capacity is there when the calendar demands it.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000004",
      "key": "a438e4f5-5119-465a-b9cc-b7c46920414a",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "heading",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Stable Operations Translate Into Enrollment and Retention"
        },
        {
          "alias": "level",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "[\"h2\"]"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorId",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000002",
      "key": "f1790109-82f4-40b5-8797-af4bb91a4571",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When <strong>academic operations</strong> hold through the pressure of peak demand, the effects extend well beyond the admissions cycle itself.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Students who receive timely responses throughout the process are more likely to complete their applications and confirm their enrollment, and less likely to disengage at any point.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In addition, <strong>student lifecycle management</strong> sustained through an external partner means students receive continuous attention, rather than <a href=\"https://centrocdx.com/the-hidden-risk-of-inconsistent-customer-responses-across-channels/\">inconsistent contact</a> whenever internal staff have capacity.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">That same consistency benefits internal teams as well. Reduced workload pressure on internal staff produces lower voluntary turnover, and lower turnover preserves the institutional knowledge that takes years to build.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://www.cupahr.org/resource/higher-ed-employee-retention-survey-findings-september-2025/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The CUPA-HR 2025 survey</a> found that staff who feel supported in their roles are significantly less likely to seek employment elsewhere. That’s a finding that points directly to the value of removing high-volume, repeating work from their responsibilities.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A <strong>student enrollment management system</strong> that holds up during peak cycles also shapes how prospective students experience an institution before they ever arrive.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The impressions formed during the admissions process follow students into their first semester, and the quality of early communication is one of the strongest signals an institution sends about how it treats the people in its care.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000004",
      "key": "29868d34-8fb6-432a-b680-c5fd2acf43d4",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "heading",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Operational Stability Through Every Peak Cycle"
        },
        {
          "alias": "level",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "[\"h2\"]"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorId",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000002",
      "key": "f6d4a70d-d903-42a5-a5c2-ea0f8f309dc7",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The academic calendar does not change, and neither does the pressure it creates. When application volume increases, student expectations for timely communication rise; it’s time to hand the reins to a trusted partner.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Centro works with educational institutions to maintain operational stability when volume peaks.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">From enrollment communications to back-office administrative support, <strong>outsourcing education services</strong> through Centro gives you the capacity to perform consistently, even during peak seasons.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://centrocdx.com/get-in-touch/\">Reach out to Centro&#8217;s team</a> to find out how a scalable support model changes what peak season looks like for your institution."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
